n home: 3 cards, maybe 400 wide each. I'll make component width 400 (fixed), height hug. In product page: cards are 2 per row, ~610 wide. Instance resize is allowed (hug contents? if auto-layout, resizing works). I'll make component auto-layout vertical with fill-width children so resize to 610 works. Text width fills container — need textAutoResize height + width fill. With auto-layout: set text layoutAlign stretch.\n\n**C_StyleTile**: 407x289 radius 20, photo bg covering, label text top-left (36 Bold \"Casual\"). Photos: Photo_Style_* instances scaled to fill (photos are landscape ~293x220 etc.). Scale to cover 407x289, clip. Label black text at 24,24? Original: white text? In original kit the label is black bold text top-left on photo. I'll use black 36 Bold... Actually original uses Satoshi bold black. With Plus Jakarta Sans Bold 36. Fine.\n\n**C_Chip (Size)**: pill radius 62, padding 12/24, default: bg #F0F0F0 text 60% black; selected: bg black text white. Create C_SizeChip default; for selected, override fills + text color (both overridable). \n\n**C_Swatch**: 37x37 circle with border rgba(0,0,0,0.2); selected variant shows check icon white. I'll build inline with helper.\n\n**C_Stepper**: rounded 62 bg #F0F0F0, 170x52: minus icon, \"1\", plus icon. Build inline; but reuse across product & cart → make component C_QtyStepper (smaller in cart: 126x44). Component fixed 170x52; cart instance scaled? Resizing an instance with fixed layout... I'll just make two sizes via one component and a small variant — simpler: build stepper inline both places with helper function (it's fine, components exist for main things). Hmm \"Component reuse\" is a criterion; steppers inline is acceptable since I'll note component usage. Actually let me make C_QtyStepper at 170x52 and for cart just resize to 126x44 — with auto-layout inside, resize works if children use fixed sizes; resize would just shrink padding? With auto-layout fixed padding, resize forces padding violation... Figma 